   "source": [
    "LINEAR INTERPOLATION:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a03619c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Linear interpolation is a technique used to estimate missing values \n",
    "in a dataframe or series by filling in the gaps with values that lie on the stright line between knwon data points \n",
    "specifically,you can use the interpolate ()method with the method ='linear'parameter\n",
    "the method ='linear'is the default for the dataframes and it treats the index value as equally spaced "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 131,
   "id": "1c91c3b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "     A    B   C\n",
      "0  1.0  5.0   9\n",
      "1  2.0  6.0  10\n",
      "2  3.0  7.0  11\n",
      "3  4.0  8.0  12\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#creating datafrma ewith missing values:\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "df=pd.DataFrame({'A':[1,2,np.nan,4],\n",
    "              'B':[5,np.nan,np.nan,8],\n",
    "              'C':[9,10,11,12]})\n",
    "\n",
    "# applying linear interpolation\n",
    "df_interpolated=df.interpolate(method='linear')\n",
    "print(df_interpolated)"
   ]
  },
